<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>FAQ | SmartRecover</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/navbar.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/footer.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/info-pages.css">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.2/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../includes/navbar') %>

  <main class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">

      <header class="info-hero">
        <span class="info-kicker"><i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question"></i> FAQ</span>
        <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p class="info-lead">
          Straight answers about how SmartRecover works. If something here is unclear,
          visit <a href="/support">Support</a> or <a href="/report-issue">report an issue</a>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="info-card" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
        <div class="faq-list">

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What is SmartRecover?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                SmartRecover is a campus Lost &amp; Found platform built for JDCOEM students.
                It lets students post reports for lost and found items, claim found items they
                recognise, and help return belongings to their owners.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Who can use SmartRecover?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Anyone can browse open reports on the <a href="/items">Browse Items</a> page.
                To submit reports or claims you need an account. Registration asks for your
                name, email, and — like the rest of the platform — was designed for the
                campus community: a profile photo and a college ID photo are required at
                sign-up.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How do I report a lost item?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Log in, open <a href="/report">Report an Item</a>, choose the
                <strong>Lost</strong> type, and fill in the item name, description, category,
                location, and date. You can attach up to five photos. Your report then appears
                on the Browse Items page for others to see.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How do I report a found item?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                There are two ways. If the item does not match any Lost report, use the same
                <a href="/report">Report an Item</a> form with the <strong>Found</strong> type.
                If it does match a Lost report, open that lost item's details page and choose
                <em>“I Found This Item”</em> — this submits a Found report linked to that lost
                report, and the original reporter receives an email notification. Either way,
                hand the item over only after verifying the owner.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How do I claim an item?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Open a <strong>Found</strong> item from <a href="/items?status=found">Browse Items</a>
                and click <em>“Claim This Item”</em>. You will be asked for a description of the
                item (at least 20 characters), proof details such as unique markings or contents
                (at least 10 characters), a contact number, and up to five proof photos. You
                cannot claim an item you reported yourself.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Where can I see my submitted reports?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Log in and open your <a href="/profile">Profile</a>. The
                <strong>My Activity</strong> section has a <em>My Reports</em> tab listing every
                lost and found report you submitted, with its current status.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Where can I see my claims?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                In the same place: <a href="/profile">Profile → My Activity → My Claims</a>.
                Each claim shows the related item and its current status —
                <em>Pending review</em>, <em>Approved</em>, or <em>Rejected</em>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What happens after I submit a claim?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Your claim is saved with the status <strong>Pending review</strong>, and both
                you and the item's reporter receive an email with the claim reference. The
                reporter (or the campus team) then verifies ownership. SmartRecover does not
                currently provide an in-app interface for reviewing or approving claims, so
                progress beyond the status shown on your profile happens through direct contact.
                Please keep your contact number reachable.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Will I receive an email notification?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Yes, in two situations: when you submit a claim (a confirmation to you and a
                notification to the item's reporter), and when a student submits a Found report
                linked to your Lost report. SmartRecover does not currently send emails for
                registration, login, or ordinary lost/found report submissions.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Why is my uploaded image not visible?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Item photos must be JPG, PNG, or WebP, no larger than 5&nbsp;MB each, with a
                maximum of five photos. If an image still does not show, reload the page, check
                your connection, and make sure your browser is not blocking images. Private
                images (your profile photo and college ID) are only visible to you while logged
                in — that is intentional.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can I edit or delete a report?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                <strong>Not currently.</strong> Editing and deleting reports from your profile
                is not supported in this version of SmartRecover. If a report contains
                sensitive or incorrect information, <a href="/report-issue">report an issue</a>
                with the report details so the campus team can help.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How should I verify ownership of an item?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Ask for details only the real owner would know: unique markings, contents,
                serial numbers, or proof photos of the item in a private setting. Meet in a
                busy campus location, double-check any identifiers before handing the item
                over, and never share your passwords or OTPs. If something feels wrong, trust
                your instincts and <a href="/report-issue">report the situation</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What should I do if a claim is incorrect?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                If you are the reporter and receive a claim you believe is wrong, do not hand
                the item over. Reply through the contact details you have, ask for stronger
                proof, and <a href="/report-issue">report the issue</a> so the campus team can
                look into it. Never transfer an item just because someone asked.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How do I report a technical issue?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Log in and use the <a href="/report-issue">Report an Issue</a> page. Choose a
                category, describe what happened, and if possible include the page you were on
                and the exact error message. Your report is saved securely and sent to the
                support team. You can also email
                <a href="mailto:support@jdlostfound.edu">support@jdlostfound.edu</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How is my personal information used?</span>
              <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Your details are used to run the recovery process: reports show your name and
                contact details so item finders and claimants can reach you, claims are stored
                with your proof and contact number, and profile/college ID photos support
                campus-only trust. Full details, including what is stored and who can see it,
                are in the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="info-card info-contact-strip" aria-labelledby="faq-help-heading">
        <div class="info-contact-copy">
          <span class="info-kicker">MORE HELP</span>
          <h2 id="faq-help-heading">Didn't find your answer?</h2>
          <p>
            Visit the <a href="/support">Support center</a> for step-by-step guidance, or
            send the team a message directly.
          </p>
          <p class="info-contact-email">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-envelope"></i>
            <a href="mailto:support@jdlostfound.edu">support@jdlostfound.edu</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/report-issue" class="info-cta">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-bug"></i> Report an Issue
        </a>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('../includes/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
